# Marketplace: Client API (`y-mp-client`)

Use this rule for **Client** (tenant / PM company) operations on **Marketplace testing** via HTTP - especially resolving **`CLIENT`** (display name or slug) -> **`CLIENT_ID`** for **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-location.mdc`** and **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-work-order.mdc`**, and creating new clients through a reusable ask-then-approve flow.

Any saved responses, debug JSON, or scratch files: **`cursor_workspace/`** per **y-mp-ai-temp**.

## Configuration

Load secrets and URLs **only** from:

``.env.e2e.local` (repo root)`

- **`MARKETPLACE_JWT`**, **`MARKETPLACE_URL`**, **`VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL`** (optional), **`CLIENT`** (search hint), **`CLIENT_ID`** (when already known).
- **Headers** on every call: `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`, **`User-Agent`** (desktop Chrome string), **`Origin`** + **`Referer`** = **`MARKETPLACE_URL`**. Testing MP often **403** without **`User-Agent`**.

**OpenAPI:** [https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json](https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json) — tag **Client**, schemas **`ClientSearchDto`**, **`ClientSearchDtoPaginationRequest`**, **`ClientDetailDto`**, etc.

---

## Pagination quirk (same family as Location)

On **testing MP**, **`PageNumber = 0`** tends to return **HTTP 500** for client list/search endpoints checked below. Use **`PageNumber = 1`** for the first page (or omit **`PageNumber`** on **`SearchByName`** when only **`PageSize`** is needed—verify if your build differs).

---

## Read / search

### 1) Search by name (simple GET)

**`GET {api}/api/Client/SearchByName`**

| Query param | Notes |
|-------------|--------|
| **`Name`** | Substring / name filter (URL-encoded). Map from **`CLIENT`** in `.env.e2e.local` (e.g. `sandbox2` → try `Sandbox`, `Sandbox 2`, or the display string you see in MP). |
| **`IsActive`** | Optional boolean string, e.g. `true`. |
| **`PageNumber`** | **Use `1` for first page** (avoid **`0`**). |
| **`PageSize`** | e.g. `20`. |
| **`ExcludeParentClients`** | Optional per Swagger. |

Response shape: **`data.items`** — each row includes **`id`**, **`name`**, **`outboundDisplayName`**, **`token`** (public token—treat as sensitive), **`defaultAssistantId`**, etc.

Pick **`id`** where **`name`** **exactly matches** the MP client name if possible; otherwise choose the best row and confirm with the user.

**Example (placeholders):**

```text
GET {api}/api/Client/SearchByName?Name=Sandbox&IsActive=true&PageNumber=1&PageSize=20
```

### 2) Search with filters (POST)

**`POST {api}/api/Client/SearchWithPagination`**  
**Body:** JSON **`ClientSearchDtoPaginationRequest`**

```json
{
  "pageNumber": 1,
  "pageSize": 20,
  "item": {
    "name": "Sandbox",
    "isActive": true
  }
}
```

- **`item`**: **`ClientSearchDto`** — optional fields: **`name`**, **`address`**, **`email`**, **`phone`**, **`isActive`**, **`supervisorId`**, **`unAssignedSupervicor`** (Swagger spelling).
- Response: **`data.items`**, **`totalCount`**, pagination flags.

Use this when you need **structured filters** beyond a single **`Name`** query param.

---

## Read one client

### Summary row

**`GET {api}/api/Client/{id}`** — path **`id`** = numeric **`CLIENT_ID`**. Returns a **client summary** (e.g. **`name`**, **`address`**, contact fields—shape per build).

### Extended detail

**`GET {api}/api/Client/GetClientDetail/{id}`** — richer **`ClientDetailDto`** (package, flags, PM/Roo settings pointers, etc.). Prefer when scripts need onboarding / feature flags.

**`GET {api}/api/Client/GetClientLocationsAssignmentsDetail/{id}`** — locations and assignment context for that client (pairs with **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-location.mdc`**).

